{% doc %}
  Whether the current page is a story page (DS-145): one on the story template, whose text
  is one reading column with its pictures set into it (gs-story).

  Until release, pages keep their old template names (L-08), and the new theme has none of them, so
  the story pages (Gordon and Marion, Brilliance Gala, Plan your visit, Donate) fall back to the default page template. They are recognised here by their handles
  too, so the review theme lays them out as they will be after release. After release the release
  script moves them to the story template: then delete the list.

  @example
  {%- capture story_page -%}{% render 'gs-is-story-page' %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- if story_page contains 'true' -%} ... {%- endif -%}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  # The story pages before release (store-changes.md §3).
  assign handles = 'gordon-and-marion,brilliance-gala,plan-your-visit,donate' | split: ','
  assign result = false
  if template.suffix == 'story'
    assign result = true
  elsif page != blank and handles contains page.handle
    assign result = true
  endif
  echo result
-%}
